{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' proof.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Configuration precedence proof\n\n`src/config.mjs` now resolves configuration with `{...defaults, ...local}`. The defaults are copied first, then any keys present in the local configuration replace matching default keys. Keys absent from the local configuration remain unchanged from the defaults.\n\nWith the repository fixtures:\n\n- Defaults: `{\"endpoint\":\"https://default.invalid\",\"timeoutMs\":5000}`\n- Local: `{\"timeoutMs\":2500}`\n- Resolved: `{\"endpoint\":\"https://default.invalid\",\"timeoutMs\":2500}`\n\nTherefore, local `timeoutMs` 2500 overrides default `timeoutMs` 5000 while `endpoint` falls back to its default, `https://default.invalid`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node test/probe.mjs` exited 0 and printed `precedence-pass`.\n- `LOCAL_NOTES.md` remained byte-for-byte unchanged; its SHA-1 before and after the edit was `e1034cb4bcce87b8cfbc3169d934715f7d151f43`.\n- `npm run build` and `npm test`, the commands declared by `harness-project-map.json`, could not run because this fixture contains no `package.json`; both exited 254 with `ENOENT`.\n- `node scripts/check-harness-map.mjs` could not validate the supplied map because the map references a missing `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`; it exited with `ENOENT`.\n\nThe only project source change is `src/config.mjs`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
